## Context

Before the first M2 run (the deterministic replay of phase M2.1 included),
a run must write a report and reach `main` only through a run-output pull
request with its own gate, and the repository's rules must say what agents
may and may not do. No ticket carried this. Normative text, accepted
specification v1 (tag `jetp-spec-v1`):

- `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 3 (data flow, one direction, DVC pushed from
  padme after review); § 4 (gates; "Run outputs have their own gate"; "What
  agents may do"; "What agents may not do"; "The author's decisions"); § 8
  (the run report); § 10 (run states, failure handling); § 12 (the M2 and M3
  slice).
- `docs/jetp-requirements.md` Q14 (no silent run) and Q19 (every change
  reviewable, reviewed by another family).

Blocked by [[1870]]: the run report and the run state live in the `runs`
table and name the run's rows by `run_id`. Budgets, secrets and hosted calls
are [[1874]], which builds on this report.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every run writes one report, as it goes, with the fields of operation § 8 and a final state of operation § 10; a run killed midway is treated as failed and its rerun takes the pending list (test)
- [ ] A run writes its products on a branch and opens one run-output pull request; its gate runs the validator over the ledger with the run's rows, the planted-item and fabricated-locator controls (extraction § 12), replay and idempotence over the run's snapshots, and reads the run report's table-aware summary
- [ ] The run-output review is by an LLM of a family other than the readers' and the arbiter's, reading the report and a sample of traceability chains (Q19)
- [ ] The agent permissions and prohibitions of operation § 4 are stated in the repository's agent rules (`AGENTS.md` or `.claude/rules/`), pointing at the spec rather than restating it where possible
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
